```python
names = [" Asha ", "", "ben", "   "]

# loop version
lengths = {}
for n in names:
    if n.strip():
        lengths[n.strip().title()] = len(n.strip())

# comprehension version
lengths = {n.strip().title(): len(n.strip()) for n in names if n.strip()}
# {'Asha': 4, 'Ben': 3}
```

| Kind | Syntax | Builds |
|---|---|---|
| list. | `[expr for x in xs]`. | a list. |
| set. | `{expr for x in xs}`. | a set (unique). |
| dict. | `{k: v for x in xs}`. | a dict. |
| generator. | `(expr for x in xs)`. | items one at a time, lazily. |

